Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance (@mech-roylance: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY
David Roylance, Massachusetts Institute of Technology. [Module index](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-11-mechanics-of-materials-fall-1999/pages/modules/) · [Complete 359-page text](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-11-mechanics-of-materials-fall-1999/3_11_f_99_coursetextbook.pdf).

The public modules develop elastic response, material structure, trusses, pressure vessels, torsion, stress/strain, beams, experimental and numerical methods, viscoelasticity, yielding, fracture and fatigue. Read the complete modules and work their problems as these questions arise. The module index and selected elasticity, stress–strain, transformation, beam-displacement and fatigue passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Some historical fatigue statements generalize endurance limits and test-frequency constraints; retain the actual material, environment, apparatus and observation domain when comparing them with current evidence.

OCW labels the associated Fall 1999 course graduate, while individual modules bear later dates: the opening elasticity module is dated January 2000. Preserve those distinctions. These openly supplied modules are not a claim that the separate Wiley book is freely redistributable. Follow OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms and separately credited component notices. Historical material-property values are examples whose alloy, condition, temperature and evidence must be checked for a real component.

The [Engineering Viscoelasticity module](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-11-mechanics-of-materials-fall-1999/d173f95347f59d59dd9b7387ab4303e7_MIT3_11F99_visco.pdf) has 38 pages and is dated 24 October 2001. Its molecular, hereditary, dynamic and temperature sections support the materials-engineering studies. [Laminated Composite Plates](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-11-mechanics-of-materials-fall-1999/f193c908ec10d95c0bc67c904b65397a_MIT3_11F99_laminates.pdf) has 18 pages; [Statistics of Fracture](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-11-mechanics-of-materials-fall-1999/f5feb5416dda31a9a35a08982ef60e18_MIT3_11F99_stat.pdf) has 20. Their metadata and selected constitutive, laminate and size-effect derivations were inspected on 30 October 2026. Read equations in the PDF when text extraction loses subscripts, signs or inequality symbols. These separately supplied modules can differ from the assembled course text.

**Return:** [Mechanical-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2).
